.TH WUW 1 "August 2026" "wuw 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wuw \- show what is happening with a runit or SysV service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wuw
.RB [ \-n " lines" ]
.I service
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wuw
prints a compact service status containing its enabled and active state,
process tree, resource use, and recent readable log messages.
It uses runit when a service directory is present and otherwise falls back to
the service's SysV init script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-n " lines"
Show at most this many recent log lines. The default is 12.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Display a usage summary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WUW_COLOR
Set to
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour in automatic mode when set to a non-empty value.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when the service is active, 3 when it is inactive or its state is
unknown, 4 when no service definition can be found, and 2 for invalid usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/service
Enabled runit services.
.TP
.I /etc/sv
Runit service definitions.
.TP
.I /etc/init.d
SysV init scripts.
.TP
.I /var/log/runit
Common location for per-service runit logs.
.SH AUTHOR
Jacek Stypuła.
